   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "How to use",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "Image Recall - Outpaint & Upscale\n\n1. Drop an image anywhere in this window (hold Shift while dropping to load its workflow instead).\n2. The panel on the node fills in everything the image recorded: checkpoint, LoRAs, prompt, negative, seed, steps, cfg, sampler. Change anything right there.\n3. Pick the mode:\n   - outpaint: grow the picture to the chosen aspect at SDXL size (1344x768 for 16:9). About one normal render.\n   - outpaint + upscale: then one SDXL pass at the final size (1920x1088, cropped to 1920x1080). About 3 normal renders in total.\n   - upscale: only the upscale pass on the original. About 2 normal renders.\n4. Queue. The panel's Estimate shows the cost before you run, and minutes once it has timed a run.\n\nLoRA tags: click a LoRA's tags in the panel to add them to the prompt (the first 3 triggers start on).\nResize: Step 1's width/height boxes shrink the original before outpainting (0 = fit the canvas).\n\nSeed: the dice picks a new seed now; \"after each run\" = fixed / increment / decrement / randomize.\nBlend slider (Step 1): left = keep the picture, right = the new scene eats it (past 70 it redraws the picture too).\nUpscale Shape (Step 2): auto, the picture's own shape, or a fixed ratio, with stretch or crop to fit.\nHistory: thumbnails of every image you've dropped, with their settings. Click = load, X = remove, Ctrl+wheel = size.\n\nMIXING TWO PICTURES (one picture's settings, another picture's pixels)\nLock settings (on the Mode row) keeps every setting when you drop another image; only the picture changes.\n\nA. Restyle a picture with another image's recipe:\n   1. Mode: upscale.  2. Drop the image whose look you want.  3. Tick Lock settings.\n   4. Drop the picture to restyle.  5. Step 2 Shape: 16:9 + stretch for a full 1920x1080, or auto to keep its shape.  6. Queue (about 2 renders).\n\nB. Put a picture in the middle of a new scene made with another image's recipe:\n   1. Mode: outpaint + upscale.  2. Drop the image whose look you want.  3. Subject: none (keeps its prompt exactly).\n   4. Step 1: Aspect 16:9, Original at center, Resize to e.g. 768 x 386 (smaller = more new scene).\n   5. Tick Lock settings.  6. Drop the picture to place.\n   7. Blend: about 45 for a soft edge; slide left to keep more of the picture, right to let the scene take it over.\n   8. Queue (about 3 renders).\n\nWith Lock on, the panel ignores the dropped picture's own metadata; downloaded images often have none.\n\nSpeed on 8 GB: every step runs whatever the denoise; *_2s_* / sde samplers cost 2 model calls per step; many LoRAs slow everything. Untick LoRAs you don't need."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
